KNOWNBUG gcc16
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only; passes with gcc 11-15
headers.  Reproduce by preprocessing with g++-16 -E (the predefined macros
select the code paths) and running cbmc on the .ii file.
Symptom: CONVERSION ERROR at <functional> line 654 (the __enable_if_t default
argument evaluated FALSE), dropping main.
